# Customer-visible copy

When **writing or editing** user-facing text in matched paths (not when changing code logic only):

1. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/humanizer/SKILL.md`.
2. Use **embedded mode** from that skill: return only the final copy in files/commits; no “before/after” essay unless the user asked for a review.
3. Keep dbscale **factual**: do not invent features, benchmarks, or support claims. Ask if a sentence needs a missing fact.
4. Technical docs stay **plain and neutral**; marketing/README can keep a direct voice but still pass Humanizer (no “thrilled to announce”, triads, or punchy closers).

If the user is drafting microcopy in chat, run the same skill on the draft before presenting it.
